WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.069
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this is my
Flash episode 4 video.

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:11.780
Lots of awesome stuff to talk about, we got
a Felicity Arrow Crossover, Captain Cold and

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.289
The Official Birth of The Rogues.

00:00:13.289 --> 00:00:17.150
Geoff Johns wrote the episode, the title was
Going Rogue, so anytime they do stuff like

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.970
that you know there’s going to be some extra
comic book easter eggs.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:25.290
Since there were a bunch of brand new people
that just found me this week, hello.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.430
I do Flash videos every week and all the DC
TV Shows.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.330
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.710
Careful for spoilers if you’re not caught
up.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:34.220
Starting with Top 5 moments.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:37.340
Number 5 - The Flash Is Learning To Harness
the Speed Force

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.200
The games, everyone telling him he’s not
fast enough, Harrison Wells telling him there

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.040
are still things he hasn’t learned yet.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.329
All part of a season long training montage
where he learns to do the really crazy comic

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:49.290
book things.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:51.760
Like breaking into other dimensions, traveling
through time.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.850
All very possible once he achieves a certain
level of mastery.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.600
Right now it seems like that’s a long long
ways off.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.260
It’s still a little too early to tell how
far into the Flash Rebirth Comic They’ll

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.260
go this season.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.970
So I would say we might see him do something
awesome in the mid season finale.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:03.970
They usually save the big reveals for moments
like that.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:04.970
I think it would be crazy if they just went
straight from him running fast to traveling

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:05.970
through time so I think he’ll just slowly
start approaching the speed of light.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:06.970
Maybe not even that fast.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:09.110
There is a lot of headroom between how fast
he is now and the speed of light.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.750
The traincar save almost seemed like it was
teasing him going faster.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:16.710
There are mental and physical components to
being able to access more speed force.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:18.910
So plan on seeing him as he is for a while.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:24.600
He still needs to get used to the daily grind
of fighting crime.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.710
Number 4 - The Khandaq Diamond Exhibit

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:30.350
It’s Geoff Johns, so of course we get another
major franchise tease.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.410
They did the same thing on smallville.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.390
Khandaq has also been referenced on Arrow.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:40.080
As far as I know all of the Shazam Family
characters will be introduced in the movies

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.080
first.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.830
Then we might get to see Osiris or Mary or
any of the non A-list characters.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.540
They could also show up on constantine too.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.909
Since that’s a supernatural DC Universe
show.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:54.231
I couldn’t find any direct references to
the diamond itself other than it’s just

00:01:54.231 --> 00:01:55.659
a precious artifact of the Khandaq royal family.

00:01:55.659 --> 00:01:57.060
Which is and always has been Black Adam.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:00.530
I can’t wait to find out what he’s been
doing this whole time when they get to that

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:01.530
movie.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.780
If you didn’t know, The Rock is playing
him.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:15.250
So picture a super hulked out evil version
of superman.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.510
Number 3 - Felicity Crossover

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:20.090
They made a lot of jokes about why she was
there but really I think she just wanted to

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.200
see how Barry was.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.280
The first big one was Barry telling Iris crazy
people would troll all over her Blog about

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.700
the red streak.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.701
Felicity chimes in and suddenly we remember
that she had the blog up on her screen in

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:33.239
the last episode of arrow.

00:02:33.239 --> 00:02:38.740
This is an example of what I’ll call a passive
crossover.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:43.180
Yes Felicity was an integral part of defeating
the villain.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.150
She became the moral compass for all of Team
Flash so they could figure out how to get

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.150
rid of Captain Cold.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.410
Next big crossover is the mid season finale.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.930
I don’t know that this closed the book on
their ship.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:54.700
The Flash producers have said that in terms
of romantic relationships they want to keep

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.350
it to just their characters.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:57.470
And the same is true of Arrow.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:58.810
Felicity has all the new attention she’s
getting from Ray Palmer.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:02.050
So don’t close the door on Barry and Felicity,
but don’t expect it to go anywhere.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:03.888
One of the funniest things was when shit goes
crazy and Felicity jumps in and does her hacking

00:03:03.888 --> 00:03:04.888
montage.

00:03:04.888 --> 00:03:05.888
The camera swivels around her like it does
on arrow.

00:03:05.888 --> 00:03:09.090
Stephen Amell has his super hero zoom in shots
when he’s putting the hood on.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.090
This is like Felicity’s version of that.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:12.080
In the context of the show she’s not a metahuman,
but she is on the A-Team.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.150
And once the show acknowledges you as a badass,
you start getting the action movie montage

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.150
shots.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.690
So I just laughed a little when I saw they
did Felicity’s Battle Mode scene.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.910
Also, did you notice how she just had a little
desk all set up for her there.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.989
I think that was the desk that Caitlin Snow
was playing the game on earlier.

00:03:23.989 --> 00:03:25.840
But I laughed when I saw felicity sit down
at it.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.739
I know some of you asked why she changed clothes
so many times.

00:03:28.739 --> 00:03:32.900
Not counting the super hot dress, I think
each outfit was to denote different days.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.100
Like everytime we saw her in a new costume.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.440
It was the next day.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.050
She was staying at a hotel.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.800
So she was probably visiting for a couple
days.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.550
That would also explain her special little
desk at star labs too.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:45.959
As creepy as it seemed, I think Harrison Wells
line about expecting great things from her

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.170
was just foreshadowing.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:57.890
He knows everyone’s future so he know she’ll
go on to do more awesome superhero stuff.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:01.569
Number 2 - Meet Leonard Snart aka Captain
Cold

00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:06.379
Probably going to go down as the number 2
all time best villain in Flash History.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:09.819
Not the most powerful, but the most interesting.

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:14.400
That explains why they picked a really big
actor like Wentworth Miller to play him.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.389
They need someone who can play a complicated
villain, like Harrison Wells.

00:04:18.389 --> 00:04:21.129
Another great example of a very complicated
character.

00:04:21.129 --> 00:04:24.210
In case you missed it they pretty much breeze
over his entire backstory.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:28.330
Had a dirty cop for a father who used to beat
him and his sister.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.550
Who might appear on the show eventually.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:36.419
And it drove him to a life of crime.

00:04:36.419 --> 00:04:41.830
It’s his encounter with The Flash that inspires
him to become the person Cisco appropriately

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:50.350
names Captain Cold.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.639
Did you catch his reaction when Cisco called
him that to his face.

00:04:53.639 --> 00:04:54.849
It was priceless.

00:04:54.849 --> 00:05:00.009
Thematically the character is also a good
example of how heroes create their own villains

00:05:00.009 --> 00:05:05.889
sometimes.

00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:17.050
I’ve said it before, The Flash’s life
when you zoom out to scale is a big causality

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.050
loop.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.159
Something very specific happened to turn him
into the Flash.

00:05:20.159 --> 00:05:23.449
It wasn’t by random chance and it wasn’t
something that would have happened naturally

00:05:23.449 --> 00:05:25.509
without external intervention.

00:05:25.509 --> 00:05:28.270
Harrison Wells caused the big accident on
purpose.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:31.139
In the episode Cisco without thinking about
it, helps to create captain cold.

00:05:31.139 --> 00:05:35.029
Without that Cold Gun, he wouldn’t have
been able to fight The Flash.

00:05:35.029 --> 00:05:39.949
This will all make more sense at the end of
the season, trust me.

00:05:39.949 --> 00:05:45.949
The interesting thing to note is that Cisco
talked about creating the gun because he though

00:05:45.949 --> 00:05:51.189
Barry might turn out to be evil.

00:05:51.189 --> 00:05:52.819
We know an evil Flash.

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:54.639
So when he does show himself.

00:05:54.639 --> 00:05:57.419
They might have to get Captain Cold’s help
to stop him.

00:05:57.419 --> 00:06:00.289
Cisco said it himself, the gun is one of the
only things that can stop someone with Flash

00:06:00.289 --> 00:06:01.289
Powers.

00:06:01.289 --> 00:06:02.289
And as far as we know, there’s only one
gun.

00:06:02.289 --> 00:06:04.490
Just remember that, in the comics Captain
Cold has always been a neutral character,

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:08.009
so it’s not absurd to think he could help
out Grant Gustin if it suited him.

00:06:08.009 --> 00:06:09.429
He did leave amicably at the end.

00:06:09.429 --> 00:06:10.429
He totally could have called Cisco on his
bluff.

00:06:10.429 --> 00:06:13.020
and my Number 1 - Captain Cold Forms The Rogues

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:16.699
If the title of the episode weren’t teaser
enough, the same man who brought him the cold

00:06:16.699 --> 00:06:18.440
gun brought him the heat gun.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:22.539
Mick, the character at the end is the real
name for the supervillain Heatwave.

00:06:22.539 --> 00:06:24.860
Guess what his ability is.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:28.619
The tease came before they pulled that last
heist, Central and Keystone City will be the

00:06:28.619 --> 00:06:29.619
Rogue’s playground.

00:06:29.619 --> 00:06:32.119
So they’ll probably be in more than a few
episodes this season.

00:06:32.119 --> 00:06:35.373
And if you didn’t catch it, that motel room
at the end was in Keystone City.

00:06:35.373 --> 00:06:36.373
it’s right here on the other side of the
river.

00:06:36.373 --> 00:06:37.650
Central City and Keystone City are right next
to each other.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:40.300
Let me know though, what was your favorite
moment.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:43.809
And while you think about that, here’s some
of the easter eggs I spotted.

00:06:43.809 --> 00:06:49.969
I mentioned Khandaq and Black Adam, It’s
not so much an easter egg as something to

00:06:49.969 --> 00:06:50.979
watch out for.

00:06:50.979 --> 00:06:55.620
The colors that Felicity wears are always
chosen very carefully.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:59.669
It’s like they’re trying to inception
you into thinking about specific people and

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:02.499
sometimes they’re just a barometer for everyone’s
emotions.

00:07:02.499 --> 00:07:06.879
Like when things are chill she wears more
neutral colors, or when she first showed up

00:07:06.879 --> 00:07:09.929
in the bright colors with the streaks it looked
more like the Flash.

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:14.539
Like her outfit was saying I’m so excited
to talk to you about your big secret.

00:07:14.539 --> 00:07:18.840
So during Arrow tomorrow, just pay attention
to what she’s wearing and what that might

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:20.719
say about what’s going on in the scene.

00:07:20.719 --> 00:07:22.389
I know all the women in my twitter feed were
going crazy over that dress of hers.

00:07:22.389 --> 00:07:24.189
There's a "Hall of Heroes" in the Central
City Museum.

00:07:24.189 --> 00:07:27.460
In the comics, the city ends up dedicating
a Museum to Barry...while he's still alive.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:30.199
Right now their biggest hero is a cattle king
named Bobby McFeely.

00:07:30.199 --> 00:07:34.569
The person that made the phone call is the
person in the comics who is curator of the

00:07:34.569 --> 00:07:36.059
flash museum.

00:07:36.059 --> 00:07:39.849
Captain Cold talking about the Motor Car Diner,
that’s a place from the comics.

00:07:39.849 --> 00:07:44.500
when they were playing trivia, the host was
named Oswald Loomis, in the comics, he’s

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:45.509
the Prankster.

00:07:45.509 --> 00:07:48.239
He’s appeared in Superman and Flash comics
going way way back to the Silver Age.

00:07:48.239 --> 00:07:51.879
One of the groups names on the board was the
Jailbirds, I thought that might be a Prison

00:07:51.879 --> 00:07:53.139
Break joke.

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:56.959
Since so many of their actors they’ve cast
this season were on that show too.

00:07:56.959 --> 00:07:59.559
I think I mentioned most of the other big
easter eggs already, but if you saw any I

00:07:59.559 --> 00:08:02.149
didn’t mention just write them in the comics.

00:08:02.149 --> 00:08:04.189
Overall I gave the episode an A minus.

00:08:04.189 --> 00:08:08.149
Amazing introduction for a huge comic book
character with an amazing performance by Wentworth

00:08:08.149 --> 00:08:09.149
Miller.

00:08:09.149 --> 00:08:11.569
Can’t wait to see him back along with Dominic
Purcell.

00:08:11.569 --> 00:08:19.379
He’s playing heatwave.

00:08:19.379 --> 00:08:23.159
Felicity with Team Flash was great, you get
the sense that she would totally fit in with

00:08:23.159 --> 00:08:25.429
their team.

00:08:25.429 --> 00:08:29.149
But it’s Oliver who needs her the most,
so she’ll always be loyal to him first.

00:08:29.149 --> 00:08:32.890
The only thing that didn’t really jive for
me was the awkward relationshippy stuff.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.419
Like Eddie and Detective West.

00:08:34.419 --> 00:08:38.680
I loved that they had a funny bro moment but
I think we need to get to know Eddie more

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:42.319
before we warm up to him.

00:08:42.319 --> 00:08:46.810
As the romantic foil for Grant Gustin you’re
automatically programmed to hate him.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:52.639
And as a comic book fan, I’m just sitting
on my seat every week waiting for him to snap.

00:08:52.639 --> 00:08:55.110
The Iris character is still a bit of a mystery.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.170
I just don’t feel comfortable with her yet.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:09:02.399
I think that’s because she’s not inside
the group.

00:09:02.399 --> 00:09:10.040
Maybe Felicity seemed so much more fun because
she got to be on the inside from the start.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:13.770
She pretty much figured out what Oliver was
doing on her own before he ever told her.

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:16.129
So maybe Iris will do the same thing.

00:09:16.129 --> 00:09:20.070
I feel like keeping her ignorant for too long
will get a little boring, especially for comic

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:21.360
book readers.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.959
That aside, great episode, great rogue episode.

00:09:23.959 --> 00:09:24.959
Looking forward to many more.

00:09:24.959 --> 00:09:28.920
They haven’t been confirmed for a season
2, but the CW just announced the first episode

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:32.730
of the flash was their highest rated premiere
in the history of the network.

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:35.120
It’s not a guarantee, but yeah, calling
it now.

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:36.529
Season 2 is a go.

00:09:36.529 --> 00:09:40.640
So in case you missed it, crazy Marvel stuff
went down this morning.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:41.640
They announced all their phase 3 movies.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.980
So I added some links to that in the description.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:48.009
Tomorrow is a new Arrow episode with Ra’s
Al Ghul, so be sure to check it out.

00:09:48.009 --> 00:09:52.870
Right now click here to catch up on Arrow
and click here for last week’s Flash episode.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:55.399
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow!

